module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness outside the gate closure is falsified by a change to a DIFFERENT file and never reds** (THE WITNESS IS DECLARED, COMPILES, AND WOULD DISCRIMINATE CORRECTLY — it is routed to `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` because its module falls outside the import closure of the required gate prefixes, so the floor never prepares, offers or executes it. A later, unrelated change touches a file other than the witness's own file — a file the witness may even IMPORT — and that change FALSIFIES the property the witness was written to check. The witness never reds, because it never runs; the floor was green because it never looked. The harm is doubly silent: the witness was discovered and its existence is reported as a decline, so the census reads as coverage.)",

    "THE INVALID STATE is a claim that BINDS NO EXECUTION. Two distinct facts about the tree — a witness's authored assertion and a change's perturbation of that assertion's subject — are never joined, and no mechanism makes the join, because the first fact lives in a module the gate does not compile. The witness's file can be read, reviewed, and accepted while describing a property that the tree already does not satisfy the moment some OTHER file changes in a way that breaks it.",

    "WHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT A SLIP: every ordinary signal is compatible with the dormant witness and none of them malfunctions. The witness compiles, its source looks correct, the floor is green, and the change that falsified it is a valid edit to a file the witness never mentions. A reviewer of EITHER change sees nothing to investigate — the witness's diff is empty, and the other change's diff does not name the witness. The only join is the one the reader makes across two edits, and nothing demands that join.",

    "SPECIMEN, ALREADY MEASURED AND REPAIRED, which is what makes this a class rather than a worry. `dag/test/claim/executor_privileged_operation_witness_test.dag` witness `witness_population_tracks_the_slot_roster` asserted a transcribed `+ 4` against the host-wide privileged-operation tail. The tail grew to five elements via an edit to `dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_grants.dag` (d38d4aedcdd, #10525). The witness was `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` — `executor_privileged_operation_witness_test` is not in `required_gate_prefixes` — so the ordinary floor never executed it. Changed-witness selection did not fire, because the witness's OWN FILE did not change; the file that BROKE IT did. The growth was invisible from the `+ 4` file alone, and the change to `runner_host_grants.dag` contained no reference to any witness. Repaired in gunbc#10895 by deriving the count through `let host_wide = runner_host_wide_privileged_operations(deploy: ...).length()` instead of transcribing it, and the repair only executed because that PR happened to also touch the witness's own file.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable, held by no mechanism — the specimen was caught only because the PR that happened to repair it (#10895) also happened to touch the witness's own file, which is an execution-path coincidence rather than a detector. The floor already computes the `declined_outside_gate_closure` census count, but aggregates it into `declined` without surfacing it as a distinguished signal, so the gap between witnesses discovered and witnesses executed is computed and discarded. Surfacing that count would be a cheap detector but is currently unbuilt, so no mechanism today fires on this class.",

    "HARM: a property asserted to hold of the tree is demonstrably false after a mechanically permitted change, and the first signal that it holds no longer is the next person who reads both files and notices the contradiction. That is not a gate on any cadence and not an instrument anyone scheduled. The harm is latent until the false property becomes load-bearing — relied on by a later change, cited as established in a review, encoded in policy that depends on its truth.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS AND THE BOUNDARY IS LOAD-BEARING. `witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set` describes a witness that IS correct and whose schedule membership was never decided — the defect is the roster failed to include it. Here the witness is CORRECTLY declined by the gate closure policy: its home module genuinely falls outside the required prefixes and there is no scheduling error. The defect is that the property it asserts is falsifiable BY a change the witness does not own, and the gate closure that correctly declines it also insulates it from ever discovering that falsification.",

    "`stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit` describes a PROSE claim — an annotation, a rationale, a comment — that a correct edit elsewhere made false. The present class describes an EXECUTABLE WITNESS, which is a different harm model: the stale prose claim is silent until read, while the stale witness is silent because it was never given the chance to execute. A reader opening the stale witness file finds correct, discriminating source; nothing is wrong about the code. The defect is at the JOIN between the witness's gate membership and the falsifying change's scope, not in the witness's source.",

    "`witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red` describes a witness whose SOURCE cannot compile, so no run can evaluate it. Here the witness compiles and would execute its arms correctly if it ran — it simply never does, because its module is outside the gate's prepared subject. A compiler error on the witness would be a loud refusal; an unwitnessed falsification is silent.",

    "`check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim` describes a check whose OPERATIONAL SUBJECT is a strict subset of its DECLARED SUBJECT — the claim is about the whole tree but the check only examines part of it. The witness in this class is correct and operates on the right subject; it is the WITNESS ITSELF that is excluded from execution, not its subject narrowed.",

    "WHAT MAKES IT A CLASS AND NOT A ROSTERING-CODE DEFECT: the same shape recurs for every witness whose gate closure is tighter than the range of files whose changes could falsify its assertion. A witness about the compiler's treatment of patterns in the presence of import closures, filed in the module the closure resolves, is falsified when the interpreter changes its import-resolution behaviour in a file outside the gate closure. A witness about the floor's aggregate runtime, authored beside the floor, is falsified when a CI lane definition is shuffled into a file the floor witness never imports. The population is not one misconfigured prefix — it is the structural gap between a static closure and a dynamic perturbation surface.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE: ask what FILE CHANGES could make the witness's assertion false, and whether every such file is inside the gate closure that decides whether the witness runs. If the witness's own module is inside the closure but a change to a module it does not import could falsify it, the gate closure that correctly prepares the witness may still be too narrow to CATCH the falsifying change — and this row covers that case too, because the witness is discovered and may still not re-execute on a push that touches only the distant file. The trigger fires when the falsifying change's diff and the witness's execution set are disjoint.",

    "THE CHEAP DETECTOR NAMES A POPULATION THE FLOOR ALREADY COUNTS AND DOES NOT PRINT. Every `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` identity is a witness the tree asserts and the floor never touches. Printing that count as a distinguished line in the floor verdict — `unexecuted_witnesses: N` — would give a reader a single number to ask about, and any non-zero number is a warning: N files claim something about the tree that the run's evidence does not speak to. That line already has a home: the floor's `declined_outside_gate_closure` census count, which today aggregates into `declined` and disappears. Surfacing it as its own signal is a rendering change, not a structural one.",

    "CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable — in this class the mechanism DETECTS rather than prevents: the false assertion stays writable and is exposed when a dependency changes. After transitive-dependency-based changed-witness selection lands, a witness outside the gate closure whose imported dependency changed WILL execute, and a false assertion WILL turn red. The invalid state (falsified assertion with no red) is therefore DETECTED every time its falsification source changes. But the state remains WRITABLE: an author can still commit a hardcoded literal against a dynamic count, and if the dependency happens not to change between commit and the author's review window, the witness stays green. And if the selection mechanism stops running or the witness drops out of the selected set, the class returns in full — §4b(2) defines rung 2 as exactly that condition. The ceiling is 2 rather than 3 (mechanically preventable in the ladder sense) because the defect is in the witness's source (a hardcoded literal), not in the dependency graph: transitive selection catches the symptom but does not prevent the root cause from being authored.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: transitive-dependency-based changed-witness selection — execute every witness whose TRANSITIVE DEPENDENCIES (the set of modules the witness's import tree reaches) overlap with the set of changed files in a push, regardless of whether the witness's OWN file changed. The dependency relation is decidable: it is the same Node-tree reachability the namespace authority already computes, so selection can be computed from the import graph rather than guessed. A witness outside `required_gate_prefixes` that would never run on an unchanged head runs when a dependency it imports (or a module that module imports) is touched. SUFFICIENT for every witness outside the gate closure. THE CAPABILITY is a changed-witness selector over the import graph, keyed to transitive rather than direct file change; the artifact is any witness whose dependencies changed appearing in the floor verdict.",

    "THE TRIGGER ABOVE NAMES LESS THAN THE CAPABILITY, AND THIS RECEIPT CORRECTS IT RATHER THAN LETTING THE NARROW TEXT STAND (DESIGN section 4b(3): a trigger naming less than the capability it restores is satisfied while the capability stays dead). Transitive-dependency-based changed-witness selection reaches a falsifier that is a .dag MODULE the witness imports. It cannot reach a falsifier that is the COMPILER: gunbc#11720 landed a wall in `v1.compiler.infer` whose census was scoped to `what the required gates compile`, and `test.claim.workflow_dispatch_input_witness_test` -- outside the gate closure, byte-identical since #11468 -- stopped RESOLVING while main's floor stayed green (run 35509509831: `claims=402 declined_gate_closure=20750`). A compiler change is a dependency of every witness and an import of none, so no selector over the import graph enumerates its victims. That face is rostered on [[witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red]] (fourth specimen), whose trigger is the capability: PLAN THE ENROLLED POPULATION -- compile every claim-root file and refuse one that does not compile -- which is also the restoration trigger of `gunbc.rung_drop` `witness_floor_off_the_required_gate`. The discriminator is two-sided and stays so: a witness whose falsifier is import-reachable is covered by the selector named above once it lands and still reads as covered; a witness whose falsifier is the compiler, a data fixture or a required-field growth is not, and reads as the sibling row.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-09-26, AND IT IS THE CLASS AT POPULATION SCALE RATHER THAN ONE SPECIMEN. Twelve claims across six out-of-closure witness modules under test.claim.fabric, test.claim.runner, test.claim.fleet and test.claim.executor_privileged_operation_witness were red on main f17c19a8fb, found only because gunbc#12339 touched a path that enrolled them as changed witnesses. Six unrelated, correct changes to modules those witnesses IMPORT falsified them, none touching a witness file: #10568 (sudo elevation quoting), #11204 (retirement inhibition text), #11625 (a second fabric host), #11751 (microVM readback grants), #11762 (width derived-or-unresolved), #12011 (the srv1 microVM shakedown slot). The oldest had been silently red for about three weeks. In every case re-derivation found the CLAIM, not the fold, to be the earliest unjustified link -- transcribed counts, a one-member roster, an over-broad prohibition -- repaired in gunbc#12343, #12344, #12346, #12347 and #12348. This row's specimen witness_population_tracks_the_slot_roster reddened AGAIN, by a different term (#11751) than the one its earlier repair derived, which is the recurrence the next-rung trigger above exists to catch: transitive-dependency changed-witness selection would have run each of these on the PR that falsified it.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-01 (calm-hawk-793), A DELIBERATE CHANGE IN ONE STAGE REDDENING A CONTROL IN ANOTHER, AND THE CONTROL WAS AN ACCEPTING CONTROL, NOT A WALL. gunbc#12290 (std.kind, 2026-09-26) made a declared-inhabitant roster member's derived type its KIND, an Atom; v2.compiler.infer algebra_ref_is_grounded refused every Atom, so canonical_grounding_for_node refused every roster member before coercion and v2.test.manual.ingest_bridge ingest_identity_coercion_accepts_source_present_in_authored_roster went red (bisected on BuildBuddy, path-restricted: first bad 21f4d0c390). At that commit required_gate_prefixes held no v2.test. prefix, so the control was declined outside the gate closure and #12290 landed green; it stayed red about five days, found only by executing the #12860 population. Re-derivation found the earliest unjustified link in the GROUNDING PREDICATE, under-specified for the case #12290 introduced, not in the kind derivation: the predicate now admits an Atom only when std.kind kind_denoted_by_node recognises it as that authority's mint. Three more specimens in the same population had the same shape, a correct change elsewhere and an out-of-gate claim that never ran: #12625 (a metadata edge entered the roster index), #12566 (an undeclared formal became a counted advisory) and #12048 (imports became chain bindings).",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-04 (swift-bat-688), THE REMAINDER OF THE CLAIM-ROOT CENSUS TRIAGED FILE BY FILE, AND FOUR FILES ARE LEFT RED ON PURPOSE AND NAMED. REPAIRED, each run before and after with claim_batch on BuildBuddy: dag/test/claim/budget_tree_witness_test.dag was falsified by gunbc#12787 (2026-10-02), which gave gunbc.harness.harness_conversation_fork KvPrefixResidency a second variant named Evicted; the witness matches Evicted bare against product.budget_tree BudgetReconciliation, two declarers leave the gate no provider to derive, and the roster row for the pair went stale. The witness now imports its names from product.budget_tree, Evicted among them, and passes 9 of 9. Five more files were refused only for one unrostered name each beside LiveTreeDisposition and pass with full headers: ci_runner_target_witness_test 10 of 10, ebay_listing_witness_test 14 of 14, unit_standing_witness_test 13 of 13, roadmap_launch_deployment_receipt_witness_test 48 of 48, source_root_tagging_test 1 of 1. src/v2/test/claim/body_lowering/data_initializer_fn_value_test.dag failed 3 of 3 on main 5565148a55 and passes 3 of 3 on main 623eb3b32f with only the import, so a main change repaired it while nobody was running it, which is this class in the benign direction and no more observed than the breakage was. LEFT RED, NOT REPAIRED, AND WHY EACH IS NOT A SILENT SKIP. dag/test/claim/cli_dispatch_surface_witness_test.dag interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional is a DECLARED expected red (v2.workflow.floor_expected_red) whose own annotation says to keep it enrolled; the other 18 claims pass. src/v2/test/claim/body_lowering/single_arm_match_test.dag two_arm_match_still_accepts_holds and three_arm_match_keeps_every_arm_holds fail while four siblings pass; both identities sit in v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt, which declines them for cost and says nothing about their verdict, so a red has been standing under a cost row. src/v2/test/claim/long/cwc_resolution_probe_test.dag cwc_malformed_nary_coproduct_normalize_rejects and cwc_cwc_module_resolve_accepts fail (7 of 9 pass), and src/v2/test/claim/long/accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test.dag fails 19 of 24; both files are frozen path deferrals in gunbc.witness_deferral_freeze, which records identity only. For these three the subject is the v2 compiler (normalize and resolve verdicts over inline source, and the accumulator-copy lens), claim_batch prints no reason beside FAIL, and whether each is a compiler regression or a stale expectation is NOT established here. They are named so the reds are owned: the next step for each is the diagnostic the claim discards, which needs a probe over normalize_outcome and is its own change. REVIEW TELL: a cost-debt row or a frozen deferral is a statement about why a claim is not run, never evidence that it would pass.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-03 (silent-stag-886), AND ITS FIRST READING WAS THAT TWO ROUTES DISAGREED. On gunbc#13090 (feb95f8ed3 and 03b96ed790) `gunbc run --claim-run` over test.claim.seed_growth_admission_witness failed 3 of 7 claims while the required floor was green, and the report framed it as claim_batch and the floor giving different verdicts for one witness. They did not: the floor gave NO verdict. The module matches neither required_gate_prefixes nor required_gate_authored_modules, and the floor run on 03b96ed790 (37110271994) lists its one cost-debt identity as outside this run's universe, preparation never offered it. A green run that declined a claim is not a pass of it, and reading it as one is this class's harm at the reader. The claim route was right: all three reds reduce to seed_growth_roster_mechanical_checks_holds, whose duplicate-key conjunct was false on main ca79f2c660 because gunbc#12846 (Nat de-fork) listed v1_interpreter eval_match and match_pattern in kernel_grounding_interpreter_seed_growth_justification while gunbc#12903 already rostered them (match_arm_guard and value_depth rows), and the roster cites each declaration once. #12846 touched neither the witness nor seed_growth_admission.dag, only a module it imports, which is this row's shape exactly. The earliest unjustified link was the #12846 row, repaired by naming the two items as already justified, the convention the value_drop_binding_adaptation row states. The witness is its own discriminating control: red on ca79f2c660, green after. Gate admission of the module is the class's trigger applied to one module and is left to an operator ruling, because a gate row is a standing claim on every required run.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-04 (quiet-gull-508), AND THE FALSIFIER WAS A ONE-LINE IMPORT REPAIR TO A FILE THE WITNESS REACHES. test.claim.srv3_seeded_install_media, outside the gate closure and untouched, did not resolve on main 296061a898: claim_batch over its five claims exited 1 with two effect-summary-incomplete refusals in gunbc.srv3_host_effect_apply srv3_nbd_proxy_serve_apply, one per callee (gunbc.srv3_nbd_proxy_serve_intent srv3_nbd_proxy_serve_host_effect and gunbc.nbd_proxy_virtual_media_install actuator_image_unresolved_reason), and ran zero claims, while every required lane was green. EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY: gunbc#12114 (2026-09-23) gave the previously import-free gunbc.srv3_host_effect_apply ONE import line. That turns the bare-reference channel off for the file (the mechanism is the row bare_reference_channel_declines_a_pull_in_silence), so the two callee modules, which nothing else in the closure pulled, were no longer realized. gunbc#12205 then enrolled the ten unimported names of that file as ActiveDebt in v2.workflow.floor_unimported_bare_provider_debt_roster: the break was recorded as debt the day it could have been repaired, and a rostered pair outside the gate closure is a witness that does not run. REPAIR AT THE OWNING LINK, not at the effect join, whose refusal was correct: the module imports all ten names from their six declaring modules and the ten rows retire as ImportsFixed. EXECUTED, BuildBuddy, claim_batch built from the same tree in each dispatch, GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES forwarded by name: with the repair the entry resolves and all five claims PASS, exit 0; with both files restored to the bytes of 296061a898 (checked by digest against git) the two refusals return and exit is 1; with only the module restored and the rows left retired, the gate refuses all ten pairs as RetiredImportsFixedButCarried, so each retirement is individually discriminated. THE BREAK WAS FOUR WITNESS MODULES WIDE AND WHICH CALLEE REFUSED DEPENDED ON THE ENTRY. Run the same way over the witnesses of the other importers: test.claim.srv3_install_media_fetch (6 claims), test.claim.srv3_os_install_actuate (7) and test.claim.srv3_host_effect_apply_witness (22) each failed to resolve on the bytes of 296061a898 and ran zero claims, refusing at five, two and two call sites that between them name six of the ten rostered callees; with the repair all 35 claims PASS. The refused callee set differs per entry because it is whatever that entry closure did not happen to realize, which is why the symptom reads as several unrelated effect-modelling gaps. The witness over gunbc.host_convergence_census passes 12 of 12 on both trees and is the control that the instrument can report green on main. REVIEW TELL: an ActiveDebt row whose file sits outside required_gate_prefixes is not deferred work, it is a module nobody can run; adding one import to an import-free file owes the whole list in the same change.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-04 (swift-bat-688), THE SAME MECHANISM TRIAGED OVER THE REMAINING srv3-NAMED ROWS, AND THE POPULATION WAS FIVE FILES WIDE. The sixteen ActiveDebt rows of v2.workflow.floor_unimported_bare_provider_debt_roster whose NAME matches srv3, nbd or seeded_install (none sits under such a path; the ten that did were retired by gunbc#13275) lie in seven files that between them carried 198 ActiveDebt rows. Each file was judged by executing its witness entries, claim_batch built from the same tree in the dispatch on BuildBuddy, GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES forwarded by name, every test fn of the entry named. ON MAIN 78b4a164f6: test.claim.os_install_deduction (14 claims) did not resolve, twelve effect-summary-incomplete refusals naming exactly its three rostered callees, zero claims run; test.claim.fleet_intent_network (10), test.claim.host_phase_status (30) and test.claim.host_standup_spine (21) were refused at the entry on one, six and five UNROSTERED pairs, zero claims run, because each file carries a single import line and bare names added after the roster was seeded have no row; test.claim.compile_permit_scope_observe_witness (13) did not resolve, eight refusals inside gunbc.fleet_show_effective_read naming five gunbc.runner_unit_live_read callees, zero claims run. All of them outside the gate closure, every required lane green. REPAIR AT THE OWNING LINK, as in the receipt above: each of the five files imports every name it used bare (149 names across the four witness files, the declaring module taken from the gate hint of its own refusal; 34 in gunbc.fleet_show_effective_read) and 172 rows retire as ImportsFixed. WITH THE REPAIR all five entries resolve: os_install_deduction 14 of 14 PASS, host_phase_status 30 of 30, host_standup_spine 21 of 21, compile_permit_scope_observe_witness 13 of 13, fleet_intent_network 9 of 10. Rows retired with the files left unrepaired are refused one by one as RetiredImportsFixedButCarried (172 refusals), so each retirement is individually discriminated. LEFT ACTIVE, BECAUSE THE WITNESSES RESOLVE ON MAIN: gunbc.host_identity_access (11 rows; test.claim.host_identity_observation_witness 32 of 32 and test.claim.host_toolchain_components 7 of 7) and gunbc.assimilate.bmc_bootstrap_provision (15 rows; its witness 4 of 4). Those entries happen to realize the declarers, which is the entry-dependent luck this class turns on and not evidence the rows are safe under another entry. TWO CLAIM REDS REMAIN AND ARE NOT IMPORT DEFECTS: fleet_intent_network_topology_membership_is_an_identity_join, which could not run before the repair and so is this class a second time over, a roster in the witness falsified by fleet topology edits nobody could see red; and witness_srv1_width_drifts_from_declared_count_after_recarve in test.claim.fleet_show_effective_read_witness, whose entry reported 22 of 23 PASS on main as well. Neither is repaired here. The control test.claim.host_convergence_census_witness passes 12 of 12 on both trees. WHAT THE ROSTER CAN AND CANNOT REFUSE: every ActiveDebt row is in a file that already has imports, since the rule only fires there, so refusing on that predicate refuses the whole roster. The decidable narrowing is the claim-root file: when the rostered file is itself an entry, its import closure IS the entry closure, so an ActiveDebt pair there resolves only if some other import happens to pull the declarer, and the entry route can be run over every claim root to say which. 494 of the 770 rows still active sit in files under test/claim.",
    "THE TWO CLAIM REDS THE REPAIR ABOVE EXPOSED, RE-DERIVED (swift-bat-688, 2026-10-04), AND NEITHER IS A PRODUCT DEFECT. fleet_intent_network_topology_membership_is_an_identity_join: the fold is right and the witness did what it was built to do. gunbc.fleet_intent_network gained srv12_host_lan_endpoint in its topology on 2026-09-05 (76ee135bd3) and the roster the witness authors by name was not told, so the join reported a topology member no named row declares. The earliest unjustified link is the authored roster, repaired by naming the row; the claim is its own discriminating control, FAIL without the row and 10 of 10 PASS with it, both executed. It was red about a month and could not be seen because the entry did not resolve. witness_srv1_width_drifts_from_declared_count_after_recarve: NOT repaired, and named here so it is owned. The claim compares the 2026-07-03 fixture row (ten active units) with gunbc.runner_slot_allocation gunbc_runner_committed_width for srv1 and asserts Drifted. That was true while the derived width was five; the derivation has since moved (memory envelope from the host, per-host CPU offer) and now yields exactly ten, read by twelve temporary probes of which only the equals-ten probe passed. So the verdict function is correct and returns converged, and the claim is falsified by a model change in a module it does not own. It is also the fusion its own annotation warns against, a parse fixture joined to a live-derived count: ten equal to ten is a three-month-old observation agreeing with a new model by coincidence, which establishes neither convergence nor drift. Flipping the assertion to converged would mint that coincidence as a readback. Its stated dissolution is a post-re-carve width readback replacing the fixture row, which is a live observation of srv1 and is the trigger that owns this red.",
    "PROPOSED WALL, SHAPE ONLY, NOT BUILT (swift-bat-688, 2026-10-04): AN ActiveDebt ROW IN A CLAIM-ROOT FILE CARRIES A WITNESS-RUN RECEIPT OR THE FLOOR REFUSES. SUBJECT: a row of v2.workflow.floor_unimported_bare_provider_debt_roster whose file is a claim root, decided by the same discovery the floor already runs (the file declares at least one test fn), never by a path prefix. A file with imports that is not a claim root is out of scope, because the predicate file-has-imports is true of every row and refuses the whole roster. CARRIER: standing gains an arm beside ActiveDebt for those rows, carrying the entry it was run as, the tree it was run on as a GitRef, and the claims run; one receipt per FILE joined to its rows, not one per row, since resolution is a fact about the entry. JUDGMENTS, each a located refusal in v2.workflow.floor_unimported_bare_provider_debt beside the existing three: a claim-root row with bare ActiveDebt refuses as unwitnessed; a receipt with zero claims run refuses, because an entry that resolved and ran nothing is the state this class hides in; a receipt whose tree is not an ancestor of the head, or whose file changed since that tree, refuses as stale. The host supplies only the facts it alone can read (is the file a claim root, did it change since the receipt tree). WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH, STATED SO THE RUNG IS NOT INFLATED: the receipt is authored, so it is a transcription and not an execution, and every specimen on this row was falsified by a change to a DIFFERENT file, which leaves the receipt tree an ancestor and the file unchanged. The wall therefore closes one face only, debt enrolled in a claim root that was never run at all, which is how gunbc#12205 seeded these rows. It is rung 2 for that face and leaves the class where it was. The capability stays the one already named: plan the enrolled population, that is, the floor resolves every claim-root file and refuses one that does not, at which point this receipt arm is redundant and dissolves.",
    "THE THREE RESIDUAL REDS, CLASSIFIED (swift-bat-688, 2026-10-04, claim_batch on BuildBuddy, GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES forwarded). (1) `v2.test.claim.body_lowering.single_arm_match` 4 of 6 is a v2 REGRESSION from gunbc#13056, bisected; receipt on `match_arms_after_the_second_are_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering`. (2) `v2.test.long.cwc_resolution_probe` 7 of 9: `cwc_malformed_nary_coproduct_normalize_rejects` and `cwc_malformed_nary_coproduct_fail_open_control` are each other's negation, so exactly one is red by construction; that pair is a STALE EXPECTATION SHAPE (a declared fail-open written as a permanent red, not a finding), and today normalize accepts the malformed coproduct. `cwc_cwc_module_resolve_accepts` is a REGRESSION CANDIDATE, not bisected: resolve refuses with `lve_anonymous_record_expected_type_not_record` on `data review_event_wire_contract: CoproductWireContract = { ... }`, where CoproductWireContract is the one-line comma record form used in 73 corpus files; rostered as `anonymous_record_literal_refused_against_a_declared_record_type`. (3) `v2.test.long.accumulator_copy_fold_analysis` 5 of 24: the lowered Loop is still found (`quadratic_ingest_has_lowered_loop` passes) but `report_counters_state_the_domain` fails and no suspect is reported on any planted copy, so the lens no longer binds the fold carrier; REGRESSION, not bisected, rostered as `accumulator_copy_lens_binds_no_carrier`. THE COST ROW QUESTION: `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt` separates PROVEN (passed, over cost) from CENSORED (interrupted before verdict), and a censored row asserts no semantic verdict. single_arm_match sits in a CENSORED chunk. The proposed narrowing: an OBSERVED semantic FAIL must not stay represented only as a cost or censored disposition; it is a semantic red and is rostered as one. An interrupted run still establishes nothing, and nothing here promotes unknown to passing. One unbudgeted run at admission and at restoration supplies evidence at those two revisions only. It is snapshot-limited and cannot catch a regression that lands while the row stands, which is exactly how single_arm_match went red under #13056. So it supplements the existing execution and restoration obligation and does not replace it. No gate is implemented in this change.",
    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-05 (snappy-stag-806, from calm-boar-904's bisection and calm-crab-469's grammar census), AND IT STATES THE RUNG AT POPULATION GRAIN. Seven claims of v2.test.claim.value_position_whole_read were falsified by gunbc#12923 (2026-10-01); on that PR's own floor run (36893078130, FloorClean) the module's disposition was declined_outside_gate_closure, so the floor that admitted the falsifier was green because it never asked the witness. One claim of v2.test.claim.function_value_body_route was falsified by gunbc#12506 by the same route. Separately, every v2.test.parse.* module lay outside the floor's prepared universe, with seven of their claims false on main (calm-crab-469, gunbc#13372, closed; phase-1 gating is gunbc#13374). RUNG, STATED HONESTLY (DESIGN 4b(1)): for the declined population the class sits BELOW MITIGATABLE. No mechanism on the merge path executes those claims, so a falsifying change lands with no typed outcome anywhere, and that is silent wrongness rather than a rung. The decline is discovered and counted, but a count of unasked witnesses is not evidence that any of them holds. The current rung of the class is the minimum over its in-scope paths, and this path is the minimum. The per-identity population is the floor's own required_floor_disposition.tsv rows whose disposition is declined_outside_gate_closure. That file is written by the floor and not published by any CI step, so the population is not readable from a run today, and publishing it is the census's first obligation. NEXT TRIGGER, UNCHANGED IN SUBSTANCE: the capability is that every claim-root witness has a disposition that EXECUTES it on the merge path or a declared rung_drop or stall naming it. A per-change selector cannot discharge it, for the reason the compiler-wall face of witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red gives.",
